## 5. Multi-tenancy — LOCKED

### [CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY] A single ComposeServer MAY host N per-tenant ComposeIOBus objects; plugins are ALWAYS per-tenant — LOCKED PERMANENTLY

- kernel-is-sole-cross-tenant-entity: the kernel is the SOLE cross-tenant entity. Cross-tenant views (operator console, metering, audit) live in the kernel or an external tool, NEVER a plugin.
- server-namespace: `_server/*` is per-tenant.
- exceptions: exceptions require an explicit WAIVER or a redesign.
- why-this-holds: the plugin contract is UNCHANGED — a plugin remains bus-agnostic ([CXC-CS-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]). Multi-tenancy is pure kernel orchestration: instantiate N buses, bind each plugin/connector to its tenant. No plugin author does anything differently.
- deferred: access-token-per-bus is deferred as a hardening question — not yet designed.
- parked-futures: (1) VPN leaf<->root ComposeBus federation — a connector type / segment_bridge cousin, deferred. (2) Dual-emit/mirror of specific semantics across N tenant buses — the ONE sanctioned cross-tenant path if it is ever built, and it would be a kernel-mediated mirror rule, never a shared plugin. Both explicitly deferred, not designed.
- status: decided
- provenance: david-ruling — David's multi-tenancy ruling, LOCKED PERMANENTLY, on [DEC-COMPOSESERVER-BUS-STANDUP-2026-08-23].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSESERVER]
- see-also: [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL], [CXC-CS-PLUGIN-CONTRACT], [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]

### [CXC-CS-STANDUP-OWNERSHIP] ComposeServer owns the concrete standup() implementation and multi-tenant instantiation, in composeio/composeserver.py

- claim: the canonical three-step standup sequence is defined at [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]'s [CXC-CBK-STANDUP] (bare bus, attach declared connectors, load plugins respecting `requires:` floors). ComposeServer is where it is INSTANTIATED and executed, and where multi-tenant N-bus orchestration happens — a new module `composeio/composeserver.py`, NOT on `ComposeIOBus` itself.
- kernel-residue: the bus kernel itself gains only bare primitives (`attach_connector`, `connectors`, `set_liveness_oracle`, `send_message`, the hook registrars) — see [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]'s [CXC-CBK-KERNEL-PRIMITIVES]. There is exactly ONE canonical standup, never two competing sequences.
- why: [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL] — ComposeServer supervises/loads/config-persists/bus-provisions; loading and standing up plugins is its job, not the bus kernel's.
- status: proposed — awaiting ratify (Phase-0 autonomous build decision; see [DEC-PHASE0-STANDUP-AND-SERVER-OUTSIDE-KERNEL] for review)
- provenance: architect-synthesis — realizes [DEC-PHASE0-STANDUP-AND-SERVER-OUTSIDE-KERNEL] (an architect-autonomous Phase-0 build decision under David's 2026-08-23 overnight autonomy grant, recorded on that DEC node for his review).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSESERVER]
- see-also: [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL], [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSEBUS-KERNEL]

### [CXC-CS-LOADER-PUBLISHES-ANNOUNCE] The LOADER, not the plugin, publishes each plugin's derived announce + status — closing the announce-then-bind spine

- claim: ComposeServer (the loader/binder that owns `standup()`, [CXC-CS-STANDUP-OWNERSHIP]) publishes each declared plugin's DERIVED announce and status to `_server/plugins/<name>/announce` and `_server/plugins/<name>/status` on the plugin's TENANT bus, plus a `_server/status` server summary. The plugin itself never publishes its own announce — it stays bus-agnostic ([CXC-CS-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]); the loader emits it on the plugin's behalf.
- scope: LOCAL — intra-server, PER-TENANT: each tenant bus gets its own `_server/*` surface ([CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY]'s per-tenant `_server/*` lock).
- cadence: at LOAD + on-change (the [CXC-CS-DYNAMIC-SURFACE] re-announce) + PERIODIC (the loader's own BusClock tick, ~5s / `SERVER_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL_S`). PERIODIC, not on-change-only, because a MISSING publication is itself the fault report — the same discipline that closes [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND]'s announce-then-bind spine.
- caught-by: the composeio-first-bringup runtime smoke of Phase 0, 2026-08-23 — a plugin's `.announce()` was correctly DERIVED but NEVER PUBLISHED (zero callers outside its own definition, zero `_server/*` namespaces registered): a spec-conformant, statically-green plugin contract sitting over a lane with no publisher.
- status: decided
- provenance: architect-synthesis — decided and built in Phase 0, session s14 ([DEC-PHASE0-COMPOSESERVER-PUBLISHES-DERIVED-ANNOUNCE]).
- decided-in-session: composeio-hardware-architect-s14-2026-08-23
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMPOSESERVER]
- see-also: [CXC-CS-DYNAMIC-SURFACE], [CXC-CS-STANDUP-OWNERSHIP], [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL]

